`pos = cycle mod 10` (0–5 9B, 6–8 4B, 9 smol) holds on all six of today's rounds, so the closed interval was **exactly one round**: 12:30:32 → 12:40:29 ≈ **597 s**.

### The standing shortfall has WIDENED: 317 MiB, not the 188 MiB this ledger has carried since 2026-10-21

Live at write — three identical reads 12:51:17 / :18 / :19: `used 1752` · `free 6139` · util 0–2 %. Compute apps: `pid 2360` Bonsai **1470 MiB** + `pid 72233` LFM2.5-VL 134 MiB, both unleased (`--n-gpu-layers 0`) ⇒ **aux floor 1604 MiB**, up from 1498 because the Bonsai tenant restarted (pid 2812 → 2360).

`6200 + 256 headroom = 6456` against **6139 free = 317 MiB short**. The 9B rung has not fit since this floor grew; both refusals today are that same 317. This is `2026-10-15-a-moving-state-quoted-as-a-constant` reaching the shortfall itself: 188 was never a property of the 9B — it is `6456 − (ceiling − aux floor)`, so it moves whenever a CPU-offload tenant restarts.

`planner_at=planner` is again **file-existence over a retry loop**: the record was rewritten twice — `pid 127974` (mtime 12:40:29.532) then `pid 133793` (mtime 12:50:06.669, 491 B) — **both DEAD, `/proc` absent for both**, `/running` = `[]`, no model port, no planner `llama-server`. Two fresh records with dead pids 600 s apart is precisely the signature filed on 2026-10-13, re-observed.

### Forward statement, filed before the event

Counter `model_cycle_counter.txt` = **59262** ⇒ 13:00 (59262, pos 2), 13:10 (3), 13:20 (4), 13:30 (5) are all **9B** picks and are all priced out by the same 317 MiB, so **the card stays OPEN across them**; **13:40 = 59266 = pos 6 = the first 4B pick**, which fits (`3800 + 256 = 4056` against 6139, **by 2083 MiB**) ⇒ **the window closes at the 13:40 round, ≈13:40:3x, width ≈3600 s**, unless a Kev-4B acquire closes it first by taking the card itself.

**Falsifier:** free ≥ 4289 at a sample after 13:41 with a planning model resident, or a `closed` reading before 13:40 with the counter below 59266.

